{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789470802,"nonce":"Q3dQqLj1v2iZubpymPyzeR463sY=","title":"A first-call compile ran on the caller's stack, which may be a fiber's","message":"The lazy stub calls `lazy_compile` on whatever stack the first call came from. A generator body is entered on a krio fiber stack of 64 KB, and Cranelift's compile of the body ran there: `machinst::compile::compile` faulted on the guard page (SIGBUS with the fault address equal to sp) the moment the adapter's frame grew by a few hundred bytes (0e0fd61 moved the compile into the adapter). It had been within a few KB of the edge all along.\n\nFix: the first-call compile runs on a scoped thread with a 16 MB stack and the caller waits. The collector stays on: nothing in the compile touches the pool from that thread (`ZYNTAX_TRACE_GC=1` shows no \"off\" line). Cost is a thread spawn per first-call compile, invisible next to the compile.","files":null}]}